a defiant and powerful message  from iran's spiritual and political  leader ayatollah ali khamenei  the country has been under u.s sanctions  since 2018  khamenei calls them a major act of  criminality  and he took aim at former u.s president  donald trump  the maximum pressure of the united  states has failed  the previous idiots hoped to corner iran  so that it would be forced to go to the  negotiating table  and he could impose his will on weak  iran  his departure was with disgrace he  disgraced not only himself but also  the united states  the new administration of joe biden has  not lifted trump's sanctions  and khamenei says iranians now have to  work on the bases  they will not be removed anytime soon  of course we are patient and we are  doing our job if they accept this policy  that we've put forward  well everything will be all right if not  this existing situation will continue  and there is no problem with it  the message from iran has been  consistent the u.s must lift all  sanctions before it returns to its  commitments under the nuclear deal  but its breaches are of growing concern  to western powers  and the u.s is looking at iran's  presidential elections in three months  to see what kind of administration it  will be dealing with ayatullah ali  khamenei wants a high turnout at the  poles in iran to send a strong message  to the outside world  in every election iran wants to show a  picture of people queuing in front of  polling stations because  this is part of the uh establishment's  legitimacy  this is part of the picture of the  revolution that it's still  alive and that's why in the last  elections in 2020 there was a picture  the establishment didn't want the outs  outside war to see  people not turning out to the elections  maybe less than 50 percent for the first  time  iran has struggled over the last few  years its economy  currency and people have been hurt by  sanctions  but in the lead-up to the election  there's a call for optimism  this was a wide-ranging speech that  covered the economy the upcoming  presidential election and the nuclear  deal  what's apparent is ayatollah khamenei  has a deep mistrust of the united states  and wants to see actions before  iran reciprocates the situation is in a  stalemate  but a leader who's been in power for  more than three decades and seen through  several u.s presidents says  iran is in no hurry to compromise assad  beg  al-jazeera tehran
 

